# Clearpay Customer Mobile — Architecture

## Project

Clearpay **Customer Mobile** application (iOS / Android).

This is **not** the Clearpay Next.js web/admin application.

## Architecture

```
Customer Mobile
    ↓  HTTPS REST
Clearpay REST API  (/api/v1/customer/*)
    ↓
Clearpay Backend
    ↓
MongoDB
```

The mobile app **never** connects to MongoDB. There is no admin UI and no
customer web dashboard in this repository.

## Tech stack

- React Native + Expo (SDK 57+)
- TypeScript (**strict**)
- Expo Router (file-based routing under `app/`)
- NativeWind
- TanStack Query (server / API state)
- Zustand (client UI state only)
- React Hook Form + Zod
- Expo Secure Store (tokens)
- Reanimated
- Lucide React Native
- EAS Build / Submit

## Feature-oriented layout

Prefer feature modules under `features/` with shared primitives in
`components/`, API helpers in `lib/`, hooks in `hooks/`, stores in `stores/`,
shared types in `types/`, constants in `constants/`, utilities in `utils/`.

Routes live only in `app/` (Expo Router). Do not introduce a parallel
navigation tree.

## State ownership

- **TanStack Query** — anything from the Clearpay REST API (cache, refetch,
  mutations, pagination).
- **Zustand** — ephemeral client UI state (sheets, selected filters, local
  preferences that are not authoritative financial data).
- **SecureStore** — access / refresh tokens only. Never passwords.
- Do not put server entities into Zustand as a second source of truth.

## API and authority

- Consume documented Clearpay customer REST APIs only (`/api/v1/customer/*`).
- Do **not** invent endpoints, request shapes, or business rules.
- Backend is authoritative for identity, ownership, balances, payment status,
  and ledger data.
- Customer ownership is enforced by the backend from the authenticated session —
  never from a client-supplied `customerId`.
- Do not duplicate backend business logic on the client beyond presentation and
  input validation (Zod for forms).

## Hard prohibitions

- No MongoDB drivers, connection strings, or direct DB access
- No admin functionality
- No customer web dashboard features
- No secrets, private keys, or signing material in mobile source or
  `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` variables
- No mock financial data as a permanent source of truth

